# Restore procedure

## Verify repositories

```sh
sudo {{ secondbrain_ops_dir }}/bin/secondbrain-check
sudo {{ secondbrain_ops_dir }}/bin/secondbrain-restore-test ssd latest
sudo {{ secondbrain_ops_dir }}/bin/secondbrain-restore-test hdd latest
```

## Production restore

1. Stop only the `obsidian-livesync` Compose project.
2. Restore the selected snapshot into a temporary directory first.
3. Run `secondbrain-restore-test` against the restored copy.
4. Preserve the current `{{ secondbrain_service_dir }}` as a timestamped rollback copy.
5. Restore the service directory from SSD, or from HDD if SSD is unavailable.
6. Start the Compose project and verify authenticated `/_up` and the
   `{{ secondbrain_couchdb_database }}` database.

Never restore directly over the running CouchDB data directory.

